  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_25f8638d49cf4abb9fd191d637f40824",
      "statement": "Every signature in the system is computed over the frozen canonical serialization json.dumps(obj, sort_keys=True, separators=(\",\", \":\"), ensure_ascii=False).encode(\"utf-8\"), exposed as canonical_json() (with canonical_str() for hashing/logging). The form is deliberately vendored in src/haap_directory/canonical.py so the directory has no import dependency on the haap client, and it is byte-for-byte identical to the haap client package serialization: any deviation or 'improvement' breaks signature verification.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/haap_directory/canonical.py#L1-L31",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:2f09ccf7b5dba5344cde7aae05da88d1226aa36a8722b841bae94a2ae5886184:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_0807dd91d21b421095b14e7cc9358ff9",
      "statement": "crypto.py reproduces the haap client encoding conventions with raw 32-byte Ed25519 keys and standard base64 via b64e/b64d; verify_with(raw_pub, data, signature) returns False on any failure (bad signature, malformed key, or malformed signature/input) instead of raising, so callers never leak crypto internals. The directory only ever verifies agent signatures; its own KeyPair signs only directory-owned data such as challenge nonces and audit checkpoints.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/haap_directory/crypto.py#L25-L60",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:0544bb26a0c8e81fb04bf9378a1005ccb48110a0699dae1ad8b5749ab9324a8c:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/haap_directory/crypto.py#L63-L93",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ddd6f3187afe1ef131569e21a6a52d53d1abc9fc308cb17b9183aa4799417c89:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_f6af166a093a40a298731379726b92a0",
      "statement": "A fingerprint is 'HF-' + the first 16 hex characters of sha256 over the raw 32-byte Ed25519 public key, matching ^HF-[0-9a-f]{16}$ (identity.py, identical semantics to haap.identity). The directory never trusts a client-supplied fingerprint: submit_registration recomputes it from the presented public_key_b64 and rejects with FINGERPRINT_MISMATCH when it differs from manifest.agent.fingerprint, and registration completion binds the fingerprint to the key stored at challenge time, rejecting any differing re-supplied public key with KEY_MISMATCH.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/haap_directory/identity.py#L14-L26",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c6f1b7a015e5f74d212dd57b8d4f7b4410447178648bc8e464259f8d13225578:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/haap_directory/service.py#L146-L159",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9577e9ce65161387eb396cffa2ba29424d212ae1a92a4c2d8e4f00d6459faeee:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/haap_directory/service.py#L84-L102",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9d42e5d37364991ce2f413e0466f49161225d3487b4f33c64c5c97bd6964fdaf:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_2e74b3a05de9459aabc3a724d31a18b4",
      "statement": "Mutating agent endpoints have no session auth — the presented Ed25519 key is the credential. signing.verify_over(pubkey_b64, payload, signature_b64) base64-decodes key and signature and verifies them over canonical_json(payload), returning bool; signing.subset(body, fields) returns only the named fields that are present so handlers sign a defined logical subset and never include out-of-band fields (such as the signature carrier itself) in the signed bytes.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/haap_directory/signing.py#L1-L30",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:52e9f15e43f82f53f15babf1601c90681cd9e9820434f96ab01c78decbda4e56:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_b63e84a6425c414aa44c91f94f9aa479",
      "statement": "At registration an agent signs the complete manifest object: manifest_signature is a b64 Ed25519 signature over canonical_json(manifest). The directory validates the manifest, caps its canonical bytes at config.max_manifest_bytes (MANIFEST_TOO_LARGE), recomputes the fingerprint from public_key_b64 (FINGERPRINT_MISMATCH on difference), verifies the signature (SIGNATURE_MISMATCH), then issues a single-use proof-of-endpoint challenge whose nonce has the ASCII prefix 'v1:register:'. The second step requires endpoint_proof to be a b64 Ed25519 signature over the ASCII nonce bytes made by the challenge-bound key (PROOF_INVALID otherwise) before the entry is listed.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/haap_directory/service.py#L146-L168",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:db48e1dcecb94710b8b31a6b67267d25c186ceff541f00c2378fc3d683ebc84c:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/haap_directory/service.py#L84-L132",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:2add74c3653a3c931b66f4eb6ee6e31b3a1f2805932d23c5a0216b12a459c74c:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_a6a9b1c09e0342d0a09956347db5bd96",
      "statement": "Signed v1 heartbeats verify a b64 Ed25519 signature over the ASCII string 'heartbeat:{fingerprint}:{timestamp}' (not canonical JSON) using the agent's registered key; the RFC 3339 timestamp must be within ±300 s of server time (STALE_TIMESTAMP). Signature failure, an unknown fingerprint, or an expired entry all surface the same UNKNOWN_OR_EXPIRED error so the endpoint never confirms whether a fingerprint exists to callers that cannot sign.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/haap_directory/service.py#L188-L217",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:00321bdb974b2abec4df59cc85d376380b7c87cdbe0506d9e4fc1c2a56bf11be:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_bdabbeb86156479da825d9e751790917",
      "statement": "L2 domain-verification requests sign only a defined subset of the body: POST /v1/verify-domain verifies the signature over canonical_json(subset(body, ('fingerprint','domain','method'))) and POST /v1/verify-domain/confirm over canonical_json(subset(body, ('fingerprint','verification_id'))); the verifying key is looked up from the store row of the currently live agent identified by fingerprint, so the signature must be made by the registered key of a listed agent (SIGNATURE_MISMATCH or AGENT_NOT_LISTED otherwise). Extra body fields outside the subset are not part of the signed data.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/haap_directory/domain.py#L105-L114",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:0fc7a081e1dfcef8f5661b5d6bfde0102bdf5a7dd336a9e5b32e6054a89f3fd4:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/haap_directory/domain.py#L59-L71",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5388411e11eedcf8ab0ce2c846cce19ae744bea71b4f604189edf5c041ff3d97:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_3334638bb6b146be9553aac78213340f",
      "statement": "L3 vouches and L4 reports use whole-body-minus-signature signing: handlers construct signed = {k: v for k, v in body.items() if k != 'signature'} and call verify_over with the registered public key of the acting live agent — the voucher's key for vouch creation (VOUCHER_NOT_LISTED when not live) and the reporter's key for reports (REPORTER_NOT_ELIGIBLE). Vouch revocation instead signs only the server-constructed canonical dict {voucher_fingerprint, revoked_at} with the voucher's registered key.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/haap_directory/reputation.py#L45-L71",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:24cc83893a3cb629a8cc0068a95d602ec7c324878a25500b7d2a1ceb8dcf4db1:"
        },
