    {
      "id": "claim_3b2ff2817b934541b0db0be1dab924b3",
      "statement": "The tests/conftest.py Agent helper kit mirrors the wire signing conventions exactly and serves as the worked example: sign_manifest signs json.dumps(manifest, sort_keys=True, separators=(\",\", \":\"), ensure_ascii=False).encode('utf-8') with the agent key, sign_payload signs the canonical JSON of an arbitrary request object (the L2/L3/L4 subset shape), sign_nonce signs the ASCII nonce bytes for endpoint proof, and register_agent drives the full 3-step v1 registration flow using exactly those signatures.",
      "evidence": [
