    {
      "id": "claim_db0389e0ff40456493b1b0b677902ec2",
      "statement": "Manifest validation ordering and the float rule are normative because the whole manifest is signed and canonical-JSON-serialized: floats are forbidden anywhere in a manifest — including geo latitude/longitude, which must be integer micro-degrees, and prices, which must be numeric strings or integers — and this is enforced before endpoint checks (FLOAT_FORBIDDEN). The registration service additionally rejects manifests whose canonical bytes exceed config.max_manifest_bytes (default 256 KiB) with MANIFEST_TOO_LARGE and stores the canonical UTF-8 text, making the canonical form also the storage form.",
